            <div xml:id="d207">

                <pb facs="0252" n="170" sameAs="frus:frus1911/pg170"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 339.112C42/5.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Secretary of the
                        Navy.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1911-05-26"><hi rendition="#italic">May 26,
                        1911</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to previous correspondence, I
                    have the honor to inclose for your information a copy of a dispatch from the
                    American minister to the Dominican Republic, forwarding copies of all the
                    correspondence relating to the incident that took place on April 26 [sic]
                    between the commanding officer of the U. S. S. <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Chester</hi> and the guard of the barracks in the city of Santo
                    Domingo.</p>
                <p>This Department thinks that the incident may now be considered as closed.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">P. C. Knox.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
